<title>USA: Caribbean Cigar opens Dominican facility.</title>
<headline>Caribbean Cigar opens Dominican facility.</headline>
<dateline>MIAMI 1997-01-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>Caribbean Cigar Co said it opened a 26,000-foot cigar factory on January 6 in the Dominican Republic.</p>
<p>It said the new factory is in the Pisano Free Zone in Santiago, employs more than 100 cigar makers, and should produce about 8 million cigars in 1997.</p>
<p>Production from the factory will help fill the company's back orders of its super premium cigars: Signature Collection, Havana Classico, Calle Ocho.</p>
